{"explanation":"Encryptor now resolves a persistent, distinct AndroidKeyStore AES-GCM wrapping key for all new token-key writes. It first reloads the current alias and creates it with KeyGenerator only when absent, then passes both that key and its stable identity to the current-record EncryptedKey overload. The legacy master-key alias lookup is retained in a separate resolver for legacy-record handling; Encryptor itself exposes no decrypt entry point.","review_assumptions":["The mobile module's supported Android API level includes KeyGenParameterSpec and AndroidKeyStore AES/GCM key generation.","The coordinated EncryptedKey change provides encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey, String), treats the supplied alias as the current record identity, and retains legacy decoding independently of Encryptor's write-only entry point.","Because Encryptor has no decryption entry point in the supplied source, legacy decrypt-key selection is implemented by the coordinated EncryptedKey/MasterKey paths; the retained getLegacyWrappingKey resolver preserves access to the pre-existing master alias without routing new writes through it."],"no_change_required":false,"decision":"MULTI_FILE_FIX_PROPOSED_FOR_REVIEW","confidence":"medium","edits":[{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/Encryptor.java","original_code":"import android.security.keystore.KeyProperties;
import android.security.keystore.KeyProtection;","edit_kind":"declaration","corrected_code":"import android.security.keystore.KeyGenParameterSpec;
import android.security.keystore.KeyProperties;
import android.security.keystore.KeyProtection;","reason":"Import the AndroidKeyStore key-generation parameter type needed to create the persistent current AES-GCM wrapping key.","symbol":"AndroidKeyStore imports"},{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/Encryptor.java","original_code":"import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;","edit_kind":"declaration","corrected_code":"import javax.crypto.KeyGenerator;
import javax.crypto.SecretKey;
import javax.crypto.spec.SecretKeySpec;","reason":"Import KeyGenerator so first use of the current wrapping-key alias creates an AndroidKeyStore-managed key rather than reusing the legacy key source.","symbol":"crypto imports"},{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/Encryptor.java","original_code":"    private static final String MASTER = "masterKey";
    private KeyStore mKeyStore;","edit_kind":"constant","corrected_code":"    private static final String MASTER = "masterKey";
    private static final String CURRENT_MASTER = "currentMasterKey";
    private KeyStore mKeyStore;","reason":"Define a stable, distinct AndroidKeyStore alias for current records while retaining the existing master alias for legacy-record resolution.","symbol":"wrapping-key aliases"},{"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/Encryptor.java","original_code":"    public Map<String, EncryptedKey> encryptToken(SecretKey key) throws
            NoSuchAlgorithmException, IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, NoSuchPaddingException, IOException {
        Map<String, EncryptedKey> data = new HashMap<>();

        Key mk = null;
        try {
            mk = mKeyStore.getKey(MASTER, null);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            Log.e(LOGTAG, "Exception", e);
        }

        // Encrypt token key
        EncryptedKey ekc = EncryptedKey.encrypt((SecretKey) mk, key);

        data.put("key", ekc);
        return data;
    }","edit_kind":"method","corrected_code":"    public Map<String, EncryptedKey> encryptToken(SecretKey key) throws
            NoSuchAlgorithmException, IllegalBlockSizeException, InvalidKeyException,
            BadPaddingException, NoSuchPaddingException, IOException {
        Map<String, EncryptedKey> data = new HashMap<>();
        SecretKey currentWrappingKey = getCurrentWrappingKey();

        // Encrypt token key as a current, versioned record.
        EncryptedKey ekc = EncryptedKey.encrypt(currentWrappingKey, key, CURRENT_MASTER);

        data.put("key", ekc);
        return data;
    }

    /**
     * Resolves the pre-existing wrapping-key alias for legacy records. New writes must use
     * {@link #getCurrentWrappingKey()} instead.
     */
    private SecretKey getLegacyWrappingKey() throws IOException {
        return getWrappingKey(MASTER);
    }

    /**
     * Reloads the persistent current wrapping key, creating it in AndroidKeyStore on first use.
     */
    private synchronized SecretKey getCurrentWrappingKey() throws IOException {
        SecretKey currentWrappingKey = getWrappingKey(CURRENT_MASTER);
        if (currentWrappingKey != null) {
            return currentWrappingKey;
        }

        try {
            KeyGenerator keyGenerator = KeyGenerator.getInstance(
                    KeyProperties.KEY_ALGORITHM_AES, "AndroidKeyStore");
            keyGenerator.init(new KeyGenParameterSpec.Builder(
                    CURRENT_MASTER,
                    KeyProperties.PURPOSE_ENCRYPT | KeyProperties.PURPOSE_DECRYPT)
                    .setBlockModes(KeyProperties.BLOCK_MODE_GCM)
                    .setEncryptionPaddings(KeyProperties.ENCRYPTION_PADDING_NONE)
                    .build());
            return keyGenerator.generateKey();
        } catch (GeneralSecurityException e) {
            Log.e(LOGTAG, "Unable to create current wrapping key", e);
            throw new IOException("Unable to create current wrapping key", e);
        }
    }

    private SecretKey getWrappingKey(String alias) throws IOException {
        try {
            Key wrappingKey = mKeyStore.getKey(alias, null);
            if (wrappingKey == null) {
                return null;
            }
            if (!(wrappingKey instanceof SecretKey)) {
                throw new IOException("AndroidKeyStore alias does not contain a secret key: " + alias);
            }
            return (SecretKey) wrappingKey;
        } catch (GeneralSecurityException e) {
            Log.e(LOGTAG, "Unable to load wrapping key", e);
            throw new IOException("Unable to load wrapping key", e);
        }
    }","reason":"Route new encryption through a generated, persistent current AndroidKeyStore key and its alias-based record identity. Preserve the legacy master-alias lookup as an explicit resolver, and convert keystore failures into the already-declared IOException contract rather than silently passing a null key to encryption.","symbol":"Encryptor.encryptToken and wrapping-key lookup/creation path"}],"manual_review_required":true,"provided_contracts":["encryptToken(SecretKey) retains its public signature and now always writes through EncryptedKey.encrypt(SecretKey, SecretKey, String) using the persistent current alias currentMasterKey.","The current wrapping key is reloaded from AndroidKeyStore when present and is created through AndroidKeyStore KeyGenerator with AES/GCM encrypt/decrypt purposes only when the current alias is absent.","The existing masterKey alias remains resolvable through getLegacyWrappingKey() for legacy-record handling and is not used for new writes."],"required_contracts":["EncryptedKey must provide encrypt(SecretKey wrappingKey, SecretKey plaintext, String wrappingKeyId) and encode current records with the supplied non-empty wrapping-key identity.","EncryptedKey and MasterKey must retain selection of the legacy key for records without the current discriminator and select a generated current key by the stored wrapping-key identity for current records.","The dedicated instrumentation tests must verify current Encryptor writes use the current generated-key lifecycle and that legacy representations remain decryptable through the coordinated legacy paths."],"source_file_path":"mobile/src/main/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/Encryptor.java","required_tests":["In mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKeyTest.java, verify current generated-key encryption/decryption round trips and reuse of the same persistent current wrapping-key identity.","In mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKeyTest.java, verify repeated current writes retain distinct AES-GCM parameters while decrypting successfully.","In mobile/src/androidTest/java/org/fedorahosted/freeotp/encryptor/EncryptedKeyTest.java, verify representative legacy-format records remain decryptable through the retained legacy key path.","Run Android-test source compilation and the mobile module test tasks after all coordinated files are applied."]}
